\paragraph{Pre-trained baseline (no fine-tuning).}
Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct without task-specific fine-tuning confirms the gap is model-intrinsic on CoNLL (conclusion: success; structural signals outperform surface, consistent with fine-tuned results).
On SciERC, the pretrained model fails the capability precondition: greedy F1${=}0.242$, with 46\% of samples producing F1${=}0$ (vs.\ 17.8\% for fine-tuned).
Oracle headroom is large (14.7\,pp) but irrelevant when the base model cannot produce useful partial outputs.
This establishes a scope boundary: the correlation-selection gap diagnosis applies when the model has basic task competence; below that floor, entity-level construction cannot improve over greedy because the raw extractions lack the partial-correctness needed for aggregation benefit.

